     3	
     4	Root cause this guards: the engine `AgentLoop._run` appends the terminal marker
     5	(FINISHED/STUCK/ERROR) at run end. A follow-up appended while the run finalizes
     6	lands just BEFORE that marker. The old predicate counted RUNNING/FINISHED/STUCK/
     7	ERROR StatusEvents as "progress", so the marker masked the follow-up as already
     8	processed forever — the run() re-entry + the runtime re-kick both no-op'd and the
     9	turn was stranded. With status markers excluded, only REAL work (tool calls /
    10	observations / plan events / assistant messages) consumes a turn, so a follow-up
